# Project: [name]

Copy to your project root as `CLAUDE.md` and fill in per repo — `/orient`
will offer to draft this from its codebase map. Keep it under ~50 lines;
every line loads into every session, so include only facts Claude cannot
infer from reading the code, and prune anything whose removal would not
cause a mistake.

## Commands

- Install: [e.g. `npm ci` / `uv sync`]
- Dev/run: [e.g. `npm run dev`]
- Test (single file — prefer over the full suite): [e.g. `npm test -- path/to/file`]
- Test (all): [e.g. `npm test`]
- Typecheck: [e.g. `npx tsc --noEmit`]
- Lint + fix: [e.g. `npm run lint -- --fix`]
- Format: [e.g. `npx prettier --write .`]

## Conventions

- [Style rules that differ from language defaults — at most 2-3]
- [Commit format and branch naming]

## Verification

- After any code change, run [typecheck] and the relevant test file before
  reporting done. Show the command output, not a claim that it passed.

